      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1392,
        "height": 672,
        "content": "# AI-Driven Supplier Discovery Workflow\n\n## How it works:\n\nThis workflow automates supplier discovery and evaluation for procurement teams. When an RFx request is submitted through the webhook, the workflow retrieves the corresponding sourcing requirements from Google Sheets, validates the request, and normalizes key criteria such as category, country, certifications, ESG requirements, diversity requirements, and supplier size. It then searches a supplier master database for matching suppliers and uses Google Gemini to assess supplier fit based on sourcing requirements and supplier attributes. Additional supplier intelligence data is retrieved and combined with the AI assessment to calculate a final supplier score using factors such as AI fit, ESG performance, supplier diversity, business maturity, and financial risk. Suppliers are ranked, the top candidates are shortlisted, and the results are emailed to procurement stakeholders while also being logged to Google Sheets for future analysis and audit tracking.\n\n## Setup steps:\n\n1. Configure the RFx Request Webhook endpoint\n2. Connect Google Sheets credentials for sourcing requests, supplier master data, and shortlist logging\n3. Configure Google Gemini API credentials\n4. Connect Gmail credentials for supplier recommendation notifications\n5. Configure the Supplier Intelligence API endpoint or replace the placeholder URL with your supplier intelligence service\n6. Create and map the Sourcing_Requests, Supplier_Master, and Supplier_Shortlist_Log sheets\n7. Verify supplier data fields such as certifications, ESG scores, diversity status, and years in business\n8. Test the workflow using sample RFx requests and supplier records\n9. Activate the workflow after validation\n"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
